      "description": "Job Opportunities |       . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Professor, Business Analytics and Information Systems (Peter J Tobin College of Business) |       . page has loaded. Assistant Professor, Business Analytics and Information Systems (Peter J Tobin College of Business) |       . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Professor, Business Analytics and Information Systems (Peter J Tobin College of Business) Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Professor, Business Analytics and Information Systems (Peter J Tobin College of Business) Salary $95,000.00 - $115,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Contract Faculty Job Number 202600032 Org Peter J Tobin College of Business Opening Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date 4/30/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Institution St. John’s University, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs across its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of online offerings. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. The College Originally founded in 1927, the AACSB-accredited Peter J. Tobin College of Business now has more than 3,000 students in a wide variety of undergraduate and graduate programs, all supported by more than 150 faculty, administrators, and staff on the Queens and Manhattan, NY, campuses. The Tobin College’s highly ranked programs are led by an outstanding faculty of teacher-scholars, widely recognized for their excellent teaching and expertise in various business areas. The Tobin undergraduate business program is ranked #50 by Poets & Quants, and our Online MBA program is ranked #42 by U.S. News & World Report. For more information, please visit: https://www.stjohns.edu/academics/schools/peter-j-tobin-college-business . The Department The Department of Business Analytics and Information Systems of the Tobin College of Business of St. John’s University is inviting applications for a non-tenure track position at the Assistant Professor level starting in Fall 2026. The Department of Business Analytics and Information Systems is a thriving, driven department with 12 tenure-track/tenured faculty members. The Business Analytics department offers the following degrees: B.S. in Business Analytics, M.S. in Business Analytics, MBA concentration in Information Systems, and MBA concentration in Business Analytics. For more information on the Department of Business Analytics and Information Systems, please visit: https://www.stjohns.edu/resources/places/business-analytics-information-systems. Commitment to Equal Opportunity St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. It is understood that any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment, and education. Job Responsibilities Responsibilities include maintaining an active research profile, teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, and contributing to the university through service, all of which are essential at the Tobin College of Business. The candidate should be able to teach a wide range of business analytics courses, from introductory to advanced levels. Our faculty engage in professional development, program development, assessment, and service to the University and broader community. Candidates should be familiar with technology-supported learning pedagogy and be able to integrate technology, particularly AI, into teaching. Furthermore, candidates should be able to use different teaching modalities, including face-to-face, online, and hybrid. Competencies, Education, Experience A DBA or Ph.D. in Data Science, Statistics, Business Analytics, or a closely related field is required for this position. ABDs in advanced dissertation stages will be considered. A successful applicant should be an effective, empathetic teacher at both the undergraduate and graduate levels and actively participate in different service-related activities. All specialization areas in Business Analytics will be considered; however, particular attention will be given to candidates with expertise in data mining, artificial intelligence, analytical computing, statistics, and decision sciences. Preference will be given to candidates who can support the growth of undergraduate and graduate programs. Supplemental Information Application Process Candidates are invited to apply online. Applicants will need to include an application letter, a resume/CV (including the names and contact information of 3 references), a teaching philosophy, and photocopies or official transcripts. Preference will be given to candidates who can support the growth of undergraduate and graduate programs. The selection process begins July 24, 2026, and continues until the position is filled. Link to Apply: Assistant Professor, Business Analytics and Information Systems Non-Tenure Track TF27-TOB-08 *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce.  Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright