    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5458108/associate-director-of-benefits": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Benefits",
      "description": "Job Opportunities |       . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Associate Director of Benefits |       . page has loaded. Associate Director of Benefits |       . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Associate Director of Benefits Print Apply ﻿ Associate Director of Benefits Salary $110,600.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600058 Org Human Resources Opening Date 08/24/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary This position reports to the Director of Benefits and is responsible for providing advanced-level administration and oversight of the University’s employee benefits programs.   The Associate Director is responsible for the day-to-day management of key benefits operations, including leaves of absence, ADA accommodations, retirement programs, and designated compliance-related benefits activities.  The Associate Director functions as a senior subject-matter expert and primary operational lead, carrying a significant casework portfolio while also serving as a strategic and operational backup to the Director.  This role supports the effective administration, compliance, and delivery of health and welfare benefits and provides guidance to employees on complex benefits matters. Job Responsibilities Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Administer and manage day-to-day benefits operations, including group health/medical/dental coverage, life insurance, disability insurance, leaves of absence, unemployment, workers’ compensation, 403(b) retirement plan, flexible spending plans, and other voluntary benefits. Serve as the primary administrator for leaves of absence, including FMLA, NYPFL, disability, and other statutory and institutional leave programs. Manage the University’s ADA accommodation process, including interactive process coordination, documentation, and compliance with applicable federal, state, and local laws. Assist with administration of 403(b) plan, including: automatic enrollments, deferral changes, non-discrimination testing, audits, government filings. Collaborate closely with partners across Human Resources, the Office of General Counsel, and other University stakeholders to ensure coordinated and compliant handling of employee matters, particularly where leaves of absence, ADA accommodations, performance concerns, and complaints of bias, discrimination, or retaliation intersect. Present and provide benefits overview at new hire orientations. Provide retirement counseling to employees, including guidance on 403(b) and supplemental retirement plans, and coordinate with plan vendors as needed. Manage the HR-administered portion of the Tuition Exchange Program, specifically overseeing outbound (export) applications for University employees. Conduct complex benefits case management, resolving employee issues with professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment. Serve as a key resource for interpreting benefits policies, procedures, and applicable laws and regulations. Assist the Director of Benefits in ensuring compliance with all applicable benefits-related laws, including the Affordable Care Act (ACA), ERISA, ADA, FMLA, and other relevant regulations. Support benefits-related reporting, audits, invoices, reconciliations, and documentation, including coordination with Payroll/HRIS, Business Affairs, and external vendors. Assist with the administration of the annual Open Enrollment process, including coordination with vendors, system updates, and employee communications. Partner with the Director on benefits projects, implementations, and process improvements. Act as a backup to the Director of Benefits in their absence or as delegated, ensuring continuity of operations. Provide guidance and support to the Benefits Representative, and assist in ensuring timely and accurate responses to employee inquiries, benefits inbox management, and data entry in Banner (the University’s HRIS). Maintain accurate and confidential benefits records in accordance with University policies and legal requirements. Competencies, Education, Experience Strong knowledge of employee benefits administration, including health and welfare plans and retirement programs. Demonstrated experience engaging in an interactive process for leaves of absence and ADA accommodations in a collaborative, well-documented, and legally compliant manner, including effectively partnering with managers and other stakeholders to assess operational needs while ensuring fair and equitable outcomes. Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple complex cases simultaneously. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Exceptional customer service and employee-facing communication skills. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making abilities. High level of discretion and experience handling confidential and sensitive information. Ability to work independently while exercising sound judgment. Effective collaboration and interpersonal skills. Proficiency with MS Excel, Word, PowerPoint. Experience with Banner HRIS systems a plus Bachelor’s degree required, Master’s degree preferred.   SPHR, PHR, SHRM or CEBS Certification a plus. Minimum of 4 years of progressively responsible experience in employee benefits administration required, including direct experience with leave management, ADA accommodations, and retirement programs. Experience working in higher education preferred. Supplemental Information Supervisory Responsibility This position does not have direct supervisory responsibility but provides functional guidance and support to the Benefits Representative and may assist the Director of Benefits in coordinating team workflows and priorities. Work Environment This position operates in a professional office environment and is required to use standard office equipment such as personal computers, printers, etc. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position.  Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.  This role may be eligible for hybrid/remote work 1-2 days per week after a 3-month orientation period, with the understanding that the person in role will be required to report to campus for trainings, workshops, and other work-related meetings or events as determined by business needs or other circumstances. Travel Travel is primarily local and may include visits to the other NY campuses. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce.  Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We ar