      "description": "Job Opportunities |       . Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Financial Aid Advisor (Federal Programs) |       . page has loaded. Financial Aid Advisor (Federal Programs) |       . page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Financial Aid Advisor (Federal Programs) Print Apply ﻿ Financial Aid Advisor (Federal Programs) Salary $66,300.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600035 Org Financial Aid Opening Date 08/05/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary The Financial Aid Advisor plays a critical role in advancing the University’s commitment to Student Success by ensuring access to financial resources, providing personalized guidance, and collaborating across departments to remove financial barriers that may impact retention and graduation. Under the general direction and reporting to the Sr. Assistant Director of Student Financial Services, the Advisor will assist in the management of key federal aid processes, including the, Federal Pell Grant program, TEACH Grant program and federal verification, while delivering exceptional service to a diverse student population. Job Responsibilities Federal Aid Administration and Compliance Collaborate with the Senior Assistant Director and Senior Associate Director to ensure the federal financial aid process is seamless and student - centered. Maintain a working knowledge of federal and state financial aid regulations and University policies. Monitor document management workflows to ensure compliance with federal requirements. Assist with the timely processing, reconciliation, and reporting of the Federal Pell Grant program. Manage the federal TEACH Grant program, including reconciliation and required reporting. Support administration of the University’s Course Program of Study (CPOS) process and related aid impacts. Verification and Aid Packaging Review and complete federal verification cases for new first - year students, ensuring accuracy and regulatory compliance. Package financial aid for transfer students admitted for the spring semester. Exercise strong attention to detail and accountability when reviewing documentation and determining aid eligibility. Professional Judgment and Student Advocacy Evaluate and apply Professional Judgment for students with special circumstances in accordance with federal guidelines. Support the equitable delivery of financial aid by accurately assessing individual student financial situations. Counseling, Service, and Student Engagement Provide individualized financial aid counseling to students and families, including guidance on aid programs and verification requirements. Serve as Counselor of the Day and provide backup support for the Student Financial Services Center. Deliver professional, responsive service to students, families, alumni, and external partners. Outreach, Collaboration, and Process Improvement Utilize data to identify opportunities for operational improvement and increased student engagement. Partner with Enrollment and other University departments to support holistic student success. Conduct financial aid presentations, workshops, and virtual sessions on financial aid topics and financial literacy. Represent Student Financial Services at recruitment and onboarding events, including Open House and Accepted Student Day (evenings and weekends required). Additional Responsibilities Perform other duties as assigned in support of departmental and institutional goals. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position. Supervisory Responsibility Assist with managing student workers Other Duties This job description is not exhaustive and may include additional responsibilities as assigned. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. Competencies, Education, Experience Ability to learn and apply federal, state regulations and university policies in support of the timely delivery of federal student aid. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. Excellent attention to detail, multitasking, and prioritization skills. Ability to manage complex conversations and resolve escalated concerns with empathy and professionalism. Effective communication and presentation skills (in-person and virtual) Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree. Experience with Microsoft Office Suite. Preferred Education and Experience: Experience with Ellucian Banner. Prior experience in higher education Additional Eligibility Qualifications Must be qualified to access Federal Student Aid systems Supplemental Information Work Environment Professional office environment. Role requires routinely uses a computer, standard office equipment such as copiers, phones/voice mail, fax, scanner, printers, etc. This individual is routinely exposed to indoor environment with moderate noise level and on occasion may need to work outside. The job is an on-campus position but must be prepared to work remotely if needed and must have access to Wi-Fi, laptop, and a cell phone. Physical Demands While performing the duties of this job, the employee is routinely required to sit, stand, and move about, to carry work, reach with hands and arms, climb stairs, communicate, and hear. The employee must occasionally lift or move up to 25 lbs. Specific vision abilities required by the employee include close vision, distance vision, color vision, depth perception, the ability to adjust focus and all-day use of a computer. Employee frequently exercises flexibility (ability to shift from one task to another). Employees routinely work within time constraints and maintain attentiveness intensity. Employees are frequently involved in social interactions that require oral and written communication. Employees are required to hear conversations in moderate noise environments. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work Full-time, Monday - Friday 8:30 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Some evening and weekend work required for enrollment events. Travel This is an on-campus position and requires daily travel to campus, occasional travel to other locations for presentations and training. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce.  Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy