    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/stjohns/jobs/5454460/director-of-the-mattone-family-institute-for-real-estate-law": {
      "title": "Director of the Mattone Family Institute for Real Estate Law",
      "description": "Job Opportunities |       . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Director of the Mattone Family Institute for Real Estate Law |       . page has loaded. Director of the Mattone Family Institute for Real Estate Law |       . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Director of the Mattone Family Institute for Real Estate Law Print Apply ﻿ Director of the Mattone Family Institute for Real Estate Law Salary $110,600.00 - $124,400.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600043 Org Law School Career Services Opening Date 08/19/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John’s University School of Law is seeking a candidate for the position of Director of the Mattone Family Institute for Real Estate Law . The Director will gr ow and manage the Mattone Institute and will be instrumental in meeting the strategic goals of student success as well as enrollment (of both JD and LL.M. students) as it pertains to real estate law focused students, thereby increasing revenue.   The Director will report directly to the Associate Dean for Career Development and Externships and will work closely with the Associate Dean for Enrollment and External Relations and the Associate Dean for Law School Advancement. Job Responsibilities The Director of the Mattone Institute will direct the day to day administration of the Mattone Institute and will be instrumental in the development and management of a Real Estate LLM program. The Director will have a focus on JD and LLM students with an interest in real estate law and will grow and manage the Mattone Institute, giving a strong and cohesive home to our various real estate initiatives.  The Director will be instrumental in meeting the strategic goals of student success as well as enrollment (of both JD and LL.M. students) as it pertains to real estate law focused students, thereby increasing revenue: Serve as Co-Director of the Real Estate LL.M. Program.  This entails the recruitment, enrollment, course development, marketing and management activities in support of the program. Work with the Enrollment Office to play an integral role in the revenue-generating process of recruitment.  This includes targeting prospective JD students to attend St. John’s because of our varied real estate offerings as well as targeting JD students from other schools to enroll in our Real Estate LL.M program.   This also includes targeting international students who practice real estate law in their home country. Various tasks may include development of stories of successful real estate law JD students, etc. Work with the Academic Dean to assess curricular needs and ensure a robust roster of advanced real estate course offerings each semester. Assist in the development of JD and LL.M. real estate courses. This includes the development of course proposals and coordination of such proposals with the Academic Dean and Curriculum Committee. Encourage appropriate students to enroll in advanced real estate courses.  This includes advising current JD and LL.M students on the various course options and educating existing JD students on the joint real estate law JD/LL.M option.   This also includes taking on the administrative role of confirming eligibility and enrolling JD students for LL.M. level real estate courses. Identify and recruit adjunct professors to teach real estate law-related courses.  This includes alumni with specialized expertise, as well as judges and other practitioners. Work with the Academic Dean to manage the JD and LL.M. adjuncts.  This includes staffing specific classes, answering questions, and assisting with ongoing course administration as needed in order to create an environment where adjunct instructors can reach their full teaching potential. Hire and manage student worker and research assistant staff for the Mattone Institute as needed. Serve as primary point person for real estate law related programs/workshops, including academic colloquia and conferences, continuing legal education, student internships and clinical training. Update resources. Manage the Real Estate Fellowship Program, including recruiting and advising on the selection of new Fellows for the Program , and working with individual Fellows to help advance their career goals. As a member of the Career Development Office, the Director will facilitate student success by counseling JD and LL.M. students on their professional development. The Director will have a focus on students with an interest in real estate law. Responsibilities will include: Assisting and advising students and alumni in all aspects of their career development. Reviewing and critiquing resumes and cover letters, preparing advisees for interviews, advising on summer, semester and post-graduate job search strategies, and following up regularly. Maintaining regular contact with students and graduates and tracking activity in Symplicity. Providing academic advising to assigned JD and LL.M. students. Regularly liaising with faculty, alumni, and administrators. Work closely with the Career Development Office employer outreach team to research and develop real estate-based student externships, internships and jobs and schedule and participate in employer meetings Work with the Alumni Office to advance engagement with alumni in the real estate industry with the aim of linking them with students for job opportunities and networking purposes, driving additional financial contributions, identifying and recruiting new Advisory Board members, and promoting loyalty to the Law School. Serve as primary point person with respect to the arrangement, organization and promotion of real estate alumni-facing events such as receptions and CLE events. Cultivate key alumni relationships through frequent contact.  Attend St. John’s Law alumni events and industry events that permit interactions with key players in order to advance these goals. Manage the administrative responsibility for the efficient operation of the Mattone Institute, including: Identifying, recruiting, and managing Alumni Board of Directors members, scheduling meetings and events with them, and regularly keeping them apprised of Mattone Institute updates Designing and approving marketing materials, with the assistance of the Communications Office Overseeing the Institute’s web presence and webpage content Overseeing a robust calendar of real estate-focused student events. Interacting with students, other administrators and faculty Monitoring progress of students Developing, updating, and reporting on program performance metrics. Managing the Institute’s budget. Serve as an advisor to the NY Real Property Law Journal and the Real Property Law Society. Supervisory Responsibility This position will recruit and manage adjunct professors teaching real estate law related classes, as well as student fellows and student workers. Competencies, Education, Experience Superior interpersonal, communication, organizational, writing and administrative skills; knowledge of the legal profession. Experience in and knowledge of real estate law practice required. Knowledge of varied technology, such as generative AI platforms, Symplicity and social media. Student advising and/or career counseling experience preferred. Strong leadership skills. Real Estate Law practice experience. Required Education and Experience: A Juris Doctor degree is required. 5 or more years’ relevant professional experience required. Preferred Education and Experience: 10 or more years’ relevant professional experience preferred. Additional Eligibility Qualifications Admission to NY state bar preferred. Membership and involvement with real estate law professional associations preferred. Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. Supplemental Information Work Environment This position operates in a professional office environment.  Attendance at student and alumni events, both on-site and off-site, is required from time to time. Physical Demands While performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to stand; move about; sit; to carry work and use controls; reach with hands and arms; climb stairs; communicate. Environmental Conditions N/A Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position. Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday.  Start and end times to be established by Associate Dean. Evening and weekend events are required from time to time. Travel Travel is primarily local.   Attendance at out-of-state conferences or events may be required from time to time. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce.  Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Acce