      "description": "Job Opportunities |       . Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Public Safety Officer/Dispatcher |       . page has loaded. Public Safety Officer/Dispatcher |       . page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Public Safety Officer/Dispatcher Print Apply ﻿ Public Safety Officer/Dispatcher Salary $25.00 Hourly Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Public Safety Job Number 202600054 Org Public Safety Opening Date 08/17/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission.? As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community.? We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.?Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Department:  Public Safety Specific Job Title: ?Public Safety Officer/Dispatcher Campus:? Queens, Manhattan Command Center Dispatcher is assigned to the Public Safety Command Center and serves as the first point of contact for all emergency and non-emergency calls across the St. John’s University global enterprise. They serve as radio, telephone and computer based dispatchers of assignments, deployment of resources, and other support services (i.e. law enforcement, fire, medical, etc.). They operate and monitor multi-channel radio, security, CCTV, and warning systems for timely detection and response to local and global events and incidents. They also perform other clerical and administrative duties related to the Public Safety Mission. This role will report directly to Public Safety Supervisors. This position supports St. John’s University’s campus safety and is the first point of contact in high-stress situations, playing a critical role in ensuring prompt, professional response to incidents. Job Responsibilities Emergency Communication and Dispatch: Receive, prioritize, and document emergency and non-emergency calls from the St. John’s campus community. Dispatch public safety officers and appropriate first responders using a two-way radio system and computer-aided dispatch software. Monitor and respond to campus fire alarms, intrusion alarms, and access control alerts. Provide exceptional customer service, information, support, and assistance to all University community members including students, staff, faculty, and guests. Additionally , ensuring that all requests for service or information are directed to the relevant person or office as required. Initiate mass notifications through the emergency notification system during certain incidents Monitoring and Surveillance: Continuously monitor campus CCTV systems, access control, and emergency notification systems. Report suspicious activity or safety hazards to appropriate personnel for immediate response. Assist in activating emergency response protocols and campus alerts as needed. Maintain continuous awareness of Department of Public Safety personnel in the field or on special assignments. Information Management and Reporting: Maintain accurate and detailed records of calls, officer activity, incidents, and responses. Assist with the preparation of incident summaries and reports for St. John’s University officials and law enforcement. Perform data entry into public safety records management systems. Campus and Community Support: Provide information and support to students, faculty, staff, and visitors regarding public safety policies, resources, and procedures. Answer questions and route calls to appropriate university departments. Demonstrate empathy, calm, and professionalism in all interactions. Engage with the various campus community departments. Be mindful of current crime trends on and around the campus grounds and take appropriate action to deter such activity. Operational Support: Test and report equipment malfunctions (radios, alarm systems, surveillance monitors). Assist in training new dispatchers and student employees as assigned. Stay updated on university safety protocols and participate in emergency drills and exercises. Maintain continuous awareness of Department of Public Safety personnel in the field or on special assignments. Stay updated on the latest emergency response protocols, security procedures, technology, University and Public Safety policies and procedures. Participate in ongoing training sessions to enhance skills related to Public Safety Dispatcher duties. Other Duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time, with or without notice. This role is additional responsibility to Public Safety Officer duties which include responsibility of a dispatcher. Command Center Dispatchers, on occasion, will be required to work operational and special event overtime assignments. Command Center Dispatchers could be asked to shift hours for a period of time to meet the minimum requirements for the department. During emergency situations, such as snow storms, Command Center Dispatchers may be required to stay past their assigned tour/hours. Competencies, Education, Experience Clear, professional verbal and written communication. Strong attention to detail and ability to multitask under pressure. Ability to maintain composure and critical thinking in high-stress situations. Discretion and adherence to confidentiality and data privacy standards. Familiarity with public safety technologies (CAD, CCTV, radio systems). Excellent computer skills and be proficient in the use of emergency communications systems, including computer aided dispatch systems, multiple two-way radio systems, alarm receivers, video monitoring systems, access control systems, emergency mass notification systems, and telecommunications systems. Ability to remain on duty until relief is available and work weekends and different shifts as required. The Command Center is operated 24/7 including weekends and holidays and requires regular attendance and punctual employee presence. Customer service oriented and provide excellent customer service in all interactions. Required Education and Experience: High School diploma or equivalent required (GED). Prefer a minimum of 5 years’ security or dispatcher experience. Must obtain New York City Fire Department Certificate of Fitness (F-01) Fire Guard Impairment, to be obtained within six (6) months of employment; the certificate must be renewed by the Officer every two years and an updated copy provided to the Executive Director of Public Safety. Must obtain American Heart Association First Aid certification within ninety (90) days of employment. Must maintain certification while employed by St. John’s University. Candidate must possess and maintain a current New York Sate Security Guard License. Candidate must posess and maintain a valid Driver License from their state of residence. Candidate must be able to perform their responsibilities while wearing an N-95 respirator mask as mandated by OSHA regulations. Candidates must be able to work on all shifts, during various hours, including weekends and holidays. Preferred Education and Experience: Associates or Bachelors degree or equivalent experience. Bilingual skills are desirable. Supplemental Information Work Environment This position is performed in a secure command center environment. This position operates in a professional office environment and Command Center Dispatchers are required to use standard office equipment such as computers, printers, phones, copy machines, etc. Physical Demands Able to sit for extended periods and work shifts that include nights, weekends, and holidays. May occasionally lift or move equipment weighing up to 25 pounds. Environmental Conditions Must be able to work during emergencies, including pandemics, active shooter, weather emergencies, etc. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work Full-time Command Center Dispatchers may be assigned different shifts 24/7, including holidays and weekends. Typical hours range from: Day Shift: 7:00am-3:00pm Nigh Shift: 3:00pm-11:00pm Overnight Shift: 11:00am-7:00am Travel None required. In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the hourly rate for this position is $25.00. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer* St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurate with your qualifications, experience, and contingent upon the departmental budget. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer. We also offer an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce. Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, faculty and staff can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstores, dining facilities, campus recreation and sporting events Any offer of employment is subject to receipt by St. John’s University of satisfactory references, verification of employment and education. St. John’s University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, age, status as an individual with a disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. St. John’s offers an extremely comprehensive benefits program to meet the diverse needs of our workforce.  Along with exceptional benefits such as medical, dental, life insurance, long term disability insurance, tuition remission, generous 403(b) employer contribution, employee assistance program, and liberal paid time off policies, employees can also enjoy St. John’s performing arts, libraries, bookstore, dining facilities, campus recreation, and sporting events. Employer St. John's University (NY) Address 8000 Utopia Parkway Queens, New York, 11439 Phone (718) 990-2000 Website https://www.stjohns.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can 