      "description": "Job Opportunities |       . Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Simulation Educator for Nursing & Health Profession Programs |       . page has loaded. Simulation Educator for Nursing & Health Profession Programs |       . page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Simulation Educator for Nursing & Health Profession Programs Print Apply ﻿ Simulation Educator for Nursing & Health Profession Programs Salary $94,000.00 - $105,000.00 Annually Location Queens Campus, NY Job Type Full-Time Administrator Job Number 202600049 Org College of Pharmacy and Health Sci Opening Date 08/17/2026 Description Benefits St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission. As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community. We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world. Job Summary St. John’s, established in 1870, has two New York City campuses; international locations in Rome, Italy; Limerick, Ireland; and Paris, France; and study abroad locations around the world. The Princeton Review and other top rankings consistently recognize the University’s outstanding academics, diverse student body, dynamic internship, and volunteer opportunities, focus on student life, and diverse study abroad offerings. St. John’s University offers more than 100 undergraduate and graduate programs in its six colleges and schools, with a growing number of programs offered online. The University is accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education and 12 other major academic and professional associations. A dedication to diversity, equity and inclusion is at the heart of our mission.? As a Catholic and Vincentian university, St. John’s is committed to institutionalizing practices of inclusive excellence to ensure that we welcome and celebrate the intrinsic worth of all members of our community.? We will become an even stronger university as we enhance equity at every level of our institution.?Our graduates will excel in the competencies and values needed for leadership and service in a rapidly evolving world . Simulation Educator for Nursing & Health Profession Programs College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences St. John's University This individual will educate, coordinate, and integrate all curricular simulation and lab activities for Nursing and other health profession programs. Organizational Structure: The individual is under the direction of the Director of Simulation. This individual will educate, coordinate, and integrate all curricular simulation and lab activities for Nursing and other health profession programs. Job Responsibilities The Simulation Educatoris responsible for planning, designing, implementing, coordinating, and evaluating simulation-based learned activities for then ursing and other health professions programs. This includes,but is not limited to: Collaborating withthe Director of Simulation and nursing & health professions faculty to create and facilitate all Simulation-BasedExperiences (SBE) of the Simulation Centerandnursing skills labs. Facilitating the learning process that creates a safe and supportive student learning environment. Educating and teaching students in the simulation center andnursing skills lab as needed. Serving as the primary educator for students in open lab s requiring additional support. Providing individual teaching and support for students for practice and remediation of technical skills and competencies,as requested by faculty and students. Evaluating student performance in the simulation and skills lab in coordination with the Director of Simulation and course faculty. Serving as the lead facilitator of orientation and training of all adjunct faculty and standardized patients as needed and overseeing performance and development. Ensuring that all simulation andskills labs are set up, torn down,and maintained on a schedule to meet the learning objectives of students. In collaboration with the Director of Simulation, confirming that all required simulation hours are completed each semester as per NYS and accreditation standards. Engaging in continuing education to maintain certification or seek certification. Incorporating International Nursing Association of Clinical andSimulation Learning (INASCL) Standards ofBest Practices and continues to ensure compliance each semester. Creating, coordinating, andparticipatingin interdisciplinary educational activities involving the College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences. Providing technical support for all equipment within the simulation center and skills labs. Assistingwith faculty development, support, and training related to the use of simulation. Collaborating with faculty/staff in reporting program activities, standards, accreditation requirements, educational concerns, and achievement of student success. Participating in activities to obtain Simulation in Healthcare (SIH) accreditation. Maintaining the simulation center and skills labs to meet CCNE and other relevant health professional accreditation standards and site visits. Aiding faculty in the development of simulation competencies and evaluation tools to achieve student learning outcomes. Recommending and researching the need to service and/orpurchase additional equipment and supplies for the simulation center and nursing skills labs. In collaboration with the Director of Simulation,creating and maintaining a weekly schedule that ensures adequate coverage for all simulation and lab activities throughout the academic year. Actively taking part in Simulation Committee meetings as scheduled. Competencies, Education, Experience Educational Requirements: Earned Master's Degree in Nursing, or other health professional degree. Must hold an unrestricted license as a Registered Nurse in NYS. CHSE (Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator) certification preferred. Minimum of 1-2 years' experience working in Simulation and skills lab teaching. Required Technical Skills Familiarity with PC and MAC platforms and the ability to learn additional software programs, including audiovisual and computerized simulation equipment. Familiarity with the Canvas platform. Advanced proficiency with MS Office (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint). Intermediateproficiencywith Adobe Suites. Advancedproficiencywith Google suite, including Google Calendar and Drive. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Exceptional planning and organizational skills. Ability to take initiative and ownership of projects. Demonstrated ability to handle sensitive issues and maintain confidentiality. Ability to work well with culturally diverse populations within an organization. Proven ability to perform duties witha high levelof professionalism, flexibility, discretion, judgment, diplomacy, and tact. Ability to multitask, adapt to changing priorities, and meet deadlines. Desired Competencies Communication. Time Management. Collaboration. Personal Effectiveness/Credibility. Flexibility/Adaptability. Supplemental Information In compliance with NYC’s Pay Transparency Act, the annual salary range for this position is $94,000 - $105,000. St. John’s University considers factors such as (but not limited to) scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, as well as market and organizational considerations when extending an offer . *Important Note- St. John’s is NOT an E-Verify Employer St. John’s offers a competitive compensation program which is commensurat